      "source": [
        "### Reading the preview\n",
        "\n",
        "Three findings reshape the M2 conclusion *if* the stricter judge is closer to ground truth:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **The M2 judge was lenient.** Under `claude-haiku-4-5`, `context_precision` drops from `1.000` to `0.598` for chunked RAG \u2014 a 40 pp gap that was hidden by `gpt-4o-mini` rubber-stamping retrieved context as relevant. The previous \"metric saturation at n=8\" was judge saturation, not pipeline saturation.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Generator quality dominates context strategy.** Same chunks, same prompt, same questions \u2014 swapping `gpt-4o-mini` for `claude-haiku-4-5` as the *answer* model lifts faithfulness from `0.756` to `0.926`. This is **more lift than switching from chunked RAG to long-context** (which only reaches `0.881`).\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **RAG + Claude is Pareto-optimal over LC + Gemini at this n.** It costs `$0.024` (vs `$0.032` for LC) and scores `+0.045` on faithfulness. The \"long-context is more faithful\" narrative from the M2 canonical run does not survive the stronger judge.\n",
        "\n",
        "Caveats before reading too much into this preview:\n",
        "\n",
        "- The same `n = 8` sample is used; `q026` and `q307` failure modes from the canonical run are still over-represented in the mean.\n",
        "- LLM-as-judge research recommends *two-judge agreement* (or three) before treating a single judge as ground truth. M3 should triangulate `claude-haiku-4-5` against at least one other strong judge before drawing the conclusions above.\n",
        "- `context_precision` and `context_recall` here are sensitive to how strictly the judge interprets \"information needed to answer\" \u2014 the gap between gpt-4o-mini (1.000 / 0.917) and haiku-4-5 (0.598 / 0.750) is partly a definitional one, not pure noise.\n",
        "\n",
        "For M2 the canonical numbers in the section above stand; this preview justifies the model-upgrade items in the M3 backlog (see `evaluation/ragas_eval/README.md`, *Model recommendations for M3*)."
      ],
      "id": "m3prev04"
    },
