   "source": [
    "## Results & discussion\n",
    "\n",
    "Headline numbers from the run (n = 8 stratified gold questions,\n",
    "`coarse_rerank` retriever, `gpt-4o-mini` answer + judge,\n",
    "`gemini-2.5-flash` long-context answer; full config in the cell above):\n",
    "\n",
    "| metric | chunked RAG | long-context | Δ (LC − RAG) |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `faithfulness` | 0.899 | 0.933 | +0.035 |\n",
    "| `answer_relevancy` | 0.713 | 0.789 | +0.076 |\n",
    "| `context_precision` | 1.000 | 1.000 | −0.000 |\n",
    "| `context_recall` | 0.917 | 1.000 | +0.083 |\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer-LLM cost (OpenRouter `usage.cost`, RAGAS judge calls excluded):\n",
    "\n",
    "| measure | chunked RAG | long-context | ratio (LC / RAG) |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| total cost (USD) | $0.00304 | $0.03063 | 10.1× |\n",
    "| total tokens | 18,476 | 114,466 | 6.2× |\n",
    "| avg cost / query | $0.00038 | $0.00383 | — |\n",
    "\n",
    "### What the per-sample table actually shows (no inference, just the numbers)\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Faithfulness:** RAG drops to `0.333` on `q026` (one sample drags the\n",
    "  mean by ~0.08); long-context drops to `0.667` on `q307` and `0.800` on\n",
    "  `q010`. The other six samples score `1.000` for both pipelines.\n",
    "- **Answer relevancy:** RAG's `q026 = 0.000` is the same outlier that\n",
    "  tanked its faithfulness on that question — the LLM produced an answer,\n",
    "  but it didn't address the question. LC stays in `0.696–0.894` across\n",
    "  the eight samples.\n",
    "- **Context precision:** saturated at `1.000` for both pipelines on every\n",
    "  sample. The metric does not separate RAG from LC at this n.\n",
    "- **Context recall:** RAG misses only on `q002 = 0.333`; LC is at\n",
    "  `1.000` on every sample (expected — full papers always in context).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Cost story\n",
    "\n",
    "The long-context arm costs **10.1× more per query** for **6.2× more\n",
    "tokens**: gemini-2.5-flash's per-token rate is higher than\n",
    "gpt-4o-mini's, on top of the larger context window. One LC sample is a\n",
    "cost outlier: `q307` only cost `$0.00053`, roughly 8× cheaper than the\n",
    "rest of the LC samples. That same sample is the one where LC\n",
    "faithfulness dropped to `0.667` — the cheap cost reflects a short\n",
    "stuffed context, and the answer couldn't be fully grounded in it. Cost\n",
    "and quality co-degraded on the same query.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Caveats before reading too much into this\n",
    "\n",
    "- `n = 8` is preliminary on purpose (cost note in\n",
    "  [`evaluation/ragas_eval/README.md`](../evaluation/ragas_eval/README.md));\n",
    "  the `q026` outlier alone moves RAG faithfulness by ~0.08.\n",
    "- The two pipelines use **different answer LLMs** (`gpt-4o-mini` for\n",
    "  RAG, `gemini-2.5-flash` for long-context) but **the same judge**\n",
    "  (`gpt-4o-mini`) and the same embedding model\n",
    "  (`text-embedding-3-small`). The +0.035 faithfulness gap mixes\n",
    "  retrieval effects with answer-generator effects — disentangling them\n",
    "  needs the generator-model ablation queued for M3.\n",
    "- **Judge variance is the dominant uncertainty at n=8.** A back-to-back\n",
    "  rerun with the same seed and byte-identical answer tokens shifted LC\n",
    "  faithfulness by 6.7 pp (`1.000` → `0.933`). RAGAS asks for n=3\n",
    "  self-consistency generations from the judge but\n",
    "  `openrouter/openai/gpt-4o-mini` silently returns n=1, collapsing the\n",
    "  self-consistency. Deltas smaller than ~5 pp on faithfulness or\n",
    "  answer_relevancy are inside the noise floor. The README documents\n",
    "  the M3 fix: switch the judge to `claude-haiku-4-5` or\n",
    "  `claude-sonnet-4-5`, which honor `n>1`.\n",
    "- Cost numbers are read from OpenRouter's `resp.usage.cost` (the amount\n",
    "  actually charged for the call), not from a static pricing table. Judge\n",
    "  calls are not instrumented and add roughly $0.10 to a full run.\n",
    "\n",
    "Out of scope for M2 (queued for M3, see\n",
    "[`evaluation/ragas_eval/README.md`](../evaluation/ragas_eval/README.md)):\n",
    "the full 50-pair sweep, generator-model ablation, all four retriever\n",
    "configs, wiring the existing NLI faithfulness scorer alongside the\n",
    "LLM-judge faithfulness, and the judge-model upgrade that would push\n",
    "sub-5 pp deltas above the noise floor."
   ]
