    "## M3 canonical: n = 30 three-arm RAGAS ablation\n",
    "\n",
    "Production-grade run committed in `evaluation/ragas_eval/results/03_three_way_n30.json` (merged PR #65). Stratified **n = 30** sample, chunker-SOTA retriever (`e5_rerank_s800_o0`), judge `claude-haiku-4-5`, three arms:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **RAG · gemini-2.5-flash** — chunked retrieval + Gemini answers\n",
    "2. **RAG · gpt-4o-mini** — same retriever, cheaper/shorter answers\n",
    "3. **LC · gemini-2.5-flash** — full cited papers, no retrieval\n",
    "\n",
    "**Headline:** long-context wins every RAGAS metric by **+6 to +14 pp** vs model-matched chunked RAG, at **~6–14×** the answer-LLM cost. Generator swap on RAG alone lifts `answer_relevancy` by **13.3 pp** (Gemini → GPT-4o-mini).\n",
    "\n",
    "The multi-config full-gold driver `scripts/run_ragas_sweep.py` (88 evaluable Q, presets `sota`/`key`/`base16`) is implemented but **not** run to completion for M3 — the report uses this n = 30 ablation instead. See scaling note in the cell below.\n"
